+---
+name: canon-backport
+description: >
+  Open (or update) a PR against gc-data-v2 or tech-gc-knowledgebase
+  when a completed story flags a canon gap. Creates a dependent
+  Monday.com task linked to the source story. Idempotent.
+category: knowledge-management
+agent: morris
+---
+
+# Canon Backport (Morris)
+
+When `complete-story` closes a story whose artifacts flag a canon gap,
+this skill opens a PR with the proposed canon update and creates a
+tracking task.
+
+## Prerequisites
+
+- `gh` CLI authenticated to `hpi-gorillacommerce/gc-data-v2` and
+  `hpi-gorillacommerce/tech-gc-knowledgebase`
+- `mcp__claude_ai_monday_com__create_item` available
+- State directory: `/home/hermes/state/morris/`
+
+---
+
+## Trigger conditions
+
+This skill fires when `complete-story` detects ANY of:
+
+1. `features/<story-folder>/refinement-report.md` contains `canon-gap: true`
+2. The PR description has a `Canon-Gap:` line
+3. The closing Monday.com comment contains the keyword `canon-gap`
+
+If none of these are present, this skill does not fire.
+
+## Step 1: Parse the gap statement
+
+Extract the canon gap description from whichever trigger source fired:
+
+- From `refinement-report.md`: find the line after `canon-gap: true` —
+  it should contain a free-text description.
+- From PR description: extract the text after `Canon-Gap:`.
+- From Monday.com comment: extract the sentence containing `canon-gap`.
+
+## Step 2: Classify target repo
+
+Use the backport helper to classify where the gap belongs:
+
+```python
+from tech_dev_agents.morris.canon_loader.backport import classify_target, TARGET_PLATFORM, TARGET_KNOWLEDGEBASE, TARGET_RUNBOOKS
+
+target = classify_target(gap_text)
+```
+
+| Target | Repo | Path |
+|--------|------|------|
+| Technical / platform invariant | `hpi-gorillacommerce/gc-data-v2` | `platform/` |
+| Operational runbook | `hpi-gorillacommerce/gc-data-v2` | `platform/runbooks/` (post-STORY-1015) |
+| Business context | `hpi-gorillacommerce/tech-gc-knowledgebase` | `wiki/` |
+
+**If the target is ambiguous** (could plausibly go in either gc-data-v2
+or tech-gc-knowledgebase), open the PR as a **draft** against gc-data-v2
+and DM Mark for adjudication. Do NOT open two PRs.
+
+## Step 3: Check for existing PR (idempotency)
+
+```python
+from tech_dev_agents.morris.canon_loader.backport import find_existing_backport_pr
+
+existing_url = find_existing_backport_pr(source_story_id, target_repo)
+```
+
+If an open PR already exists for this source story, **update it** instead
+of opening a duplicate. Use `gh pr edit` with the updated body.
+
+## Step 4: Draft the canon update
+
+```python
+from tech_dev_agents.morris.canon_loader.backport import draft_backport_pr
+
+draft = draft_backport_pr(gap_text, target_repo, source_story_id)
+```
+
+The draft contains:
+- Branch name: `morris/canon-backport-<source-story-id>`
+- PR title (capped at 70 chars)
+- PR body with gap description, proposed addition, and source citation
+
+## Step 5: Open (or update) the PR
+
+If no existing PR:
+
+```
+# Create branch from main
+gh api repos/<target_repo>/git/refs -f ref="refs/heads/<branch>" -f sha="<main_sha>"
+
+# Create/update the target file with the proposed addition
+# (additive section, never destructive)
+
+# Open the PR
+gh pr create --repo <target_repo> \
+  --head <branch> --base main \
+  --title "<draft.title>" \
+  --body "<draft.body>"
+```
+
+If existing PR found at Step 3:
+
+```
+gh pr edit <existing_url> --body "<updated_body>"
+```
+
+## Step 6: Create Monday.com tracking task
+
+Create a dependent task on the source story's board:
+
+```
+mcp__claude_ai_monday_com__create_item(
+  board_id=<source_board_id>,
+  item_name="Canon-backport PR <pr_url> for <source_story_id>",
+  group_id=<source_group_id>
+)
+```
+
+If Monday.com task creation fails (rate-limit, auth, board-id), **log
+the failure and DM Mark**. Do NOT silently swallow.
+
+## Step 7: Link back to source story
+
+Comment on the source story's PR (or closed story) with the
+canon-backport PR link:
+
+```
+gh pr comment <source_pr_number> --repo <source_repo> \
+  --body "Canon-backport PR opened: <pr_url>
+
+A canon gap was identified during completion of this story.
+The proposed update is ready for data team review."
+```
+
+## Hard rules
+
+- **Idempotent:** always check for existing PR before creating a new one.
+  Branch name `morris/canon-backport-<story-id>` is the idempotency key.
+- **Never approve or merge** the canon-backport PR. The data team owns
+  review.
+- **Never open a canon-backport PR to a `*-v2` consumer repo.** Backports
+  go to `gc-data-v2` or `tech-gc-knowledgebase`, never to pipeline repos.
+- **If the data team rejects a PR:** do NOT auto-retry. Pause
+  canon-backport for that story and DM Mark with the rejection reason.
+- **Log every invocation** to `/home/hermes/state/morris/canon-backport-log.jsonl`:
+  ```json
+  {"story_id":"STORY-N","timestamp":"<ISO>","target_repo":"...","pr_url":"...","action":"created|updated","monday_task_created":true}
+  ```
