+---
+name: start-story
+description: >
+  Canon-aware start-story for Morris. Detects domain:data-pipeline tag,
+  loads gc-data-v2 canon (source README + platform docs), attaches to
+  the seed bundle, then chains to the framework start-story skill.
+category: workflow-orchestration
+agent: morris
+---
+
+# Start Story (Morris canon-aware override)
+
+Wraps the framework `start-story` with a canon-loading prelude for
+`domain:data-pipeline` stories. Non-pipeline stories pass through
+directly to the framework skill.
+
+## Prerequisites
+
+- `gh` CLI authenticated
+- `mcp__claude_ai_monday_com__get_board_items_page` available
+- State directory: `/home/hermes/state/morris/`
+- Optional: `/home/hermes/state/morris/canon-pins.yaml` (pin sha for gc-data-v2)
+
+---
+
+## Step 1: Read Monday.com task tags
+
+```
+mcp__claude_ai_monday_com__get_board_items_page(board_id=<board>, limit=1, query_params={ids: [<item_id>]})
+```
+
+Extract the `tags` column. Look for any tag matching `domain:data-pipeline`.
+
+If no `domain:data-pipeline` tag is found, skip directly to **Step 7**.
+
+## Step 2: Identify source from repo/title
+
+Parse the story seed's `# Title` line or the `repo` field to identify the
+pipeline repo slug (e.g. `spapi-reports-v2`, `walmart-supplier-v2`).
+
+Map the repo slug to a gc-data-v2 source directory using the source map:
+
+```python
+from tech_dev_agents.morris.canon_loader.source_map import resolve_source
+src = resolve_source(repo_slug)
+```
+
+If the repo is not in the source map, transition to `needs_info` with a
+clear question to Mark: "Repo `<slug>` is not in the canon source map.
+Which gc-data-v2 source directory should it map to?"
+
+**Never guess the mapping.**
+
+## Step 3: Determine pin SHA
+
+Read the gc-data-v2 pin from the canon pins file:
+
+```
+terminal(command="cat /home/hermes/state/morris/canon-pins.yaml 2>/dev/null | grep gc-data-v2 | awk '{print $2}'", pty=false)
+```
+
+If the file doesn't exist or has no `gc-data-v2` entry, fall back to `main`.
+
+## Step 4: Fetch source README and platform cross-references
+
+```python
+from tech_dev_agents.morris.canon_loader.loader import load_canon_for_source
+bundle = load_canon_for_source(src, pin_sha)
+```
+
+This fetches:
+1. `sources/<src>/README.md` from gc-data-v2 at the pinned sha
+2. All `platform/*.md` files cross-referenced in the source README
+
+If the source README returns 404, log a warning and continue to Step 7
+without canon — the story can still proceed, it just won't have
+pre-loaded canon docs.
+
+## Step 5: Write canon to story folder
+
+Create `features/<story-folder>/canon/` and write each loaded file:
+
+```
+mkdir -p features/<story-folder>/canon/sources/
+mkdir -p features/<story-folder>/canon/platform/
+
+# Write each file from the bundle
+# e.g. features/story-871-spapi-retry-fix/canon/sources/spapi-reports.md
+#      features/story-871-spapi-retry-fix/canon/platform/pipeline-standard.md
+```
+
+File naming: use the source directory name (not `README.md`) for the
+source file, and the original filename for platform docs.
+
+## Step 6: Record canon metadata
+
+Append the gc-data-v2 commit sha to `.project`:
+
+```
+echo "gc_data_v2_commit: <pin_sha>" >> features/<story-folder>/.project
+```
+
+Append a "Loaded canon" section to the seed:
+
+```markdown
+## Loaded Canon
+
+The following gc-data-v2 canon documents have been loaded for this story
+(pinned to commit `<sha>`):
+
+- `canon/sources/<src>.md` — source-level documentation
+- `canon/platform/pipeline-standard.md` — pipeline conventions
+- `canon/platform/failure-modes.md` — failure handling reference
+
+These files are local copies. The agent should grep them for relevant
+context before making architectural decisions.
+```
+
+## Step 7: Chain to framework start-story
+
+Invoke the framework `start-story` skill with the (possibly augmented)
+seed bundle:
+
+```
+/start-story <story-id>
+```
+
+The framework skill handles all standard operations: Asana claim,
+worktree creation, branch creation, task breakdown, move to In Progress.
+
+## Hard rules
+
+- **Never modify framework skills** at `.sdlc/skills/`. This skill is a
+  prelude, not a replacement.
+- **Never guess source mappings.** If the repo isn't in `source_map.py`,
+  escalate to Mark.
+- **Always record `gc_data_v2_commit`** in `.project` when canon is loaded.
+- **Non-pipeline stories pass through unchanged** — no canon loading, no
+  `.project` annotation, just chain to framework start-story.
