+# STORY-1003: Manual Steps for Mark
+
+These steps copy the `canon-backport` skill (new) and the patched `retro` and `phase-9`
+skills into the `.sdlc` submodule and deploy them to agent VMs.
+
+## Prerequisites
+
+- You must have push access to the `.sdlc` submodule remote
+- The PR for this story must be merged into `main` first
+- Run all commands from the `tech-dev-agents` repo root
+
+## Steps
+
+1. **Copy canon-backport skill to .sdlc/skills/ (new skill)**
+
+   ```bash
+   mkdir -p .sdlc/skills/canon-backport
+   cp features/story-1003-canon-backport-retro/skills/canon-backport/SKILL.md \
+      .sdlc/skills/canon-backport/SKILL.md
+   ```
+
+   Verify: `head -3 .sdlc/skills/canon-backport/SKILL.md` should show
+   `name: canon-backport` in the YAML frontmatter.
+
+2. **Copy patched retro skill to .sdlc/skills/ (replaces existing)**
+
+   ```bash
+   cp features/story-1003-canon-backport-retro/skills/retro/SKILL.md \
+      .sdlc/skills/retro/SKILL.md
+   ```
+
+   Verify: `grep -n "8a" .sdlc/skills/retro/SKILL.md` should show the new Step 8a
+   line that emits `retro-proposal-gc-data-v2.yaml`.
+
+3. **Copy patched phase-9 skill to .sdlc/skills/ (replaces existing)**
+
+   ```bash
+   cp features/story-1003-canon-backport-retro/skills/phase-9/SKILL.md \
+      .sdlc/skills/phase-9/SKILL.md
+   ```
+
+   Verify: `grep -n "3-Question Gate" .sdlc/skills/phase-9/SKILL.md` should show
+   the new gate section line number.
+
+4. **Commit and push inside the .sdlc submodule**
+
+   ```bash
+   git -C .sdlc add \
+     skills/canon-backport/SKILL.md \
+     skills/retro/SKILL.md \
+     skills/phase-9/SKILL.md
+   git -C .sdlc commit -m 'feat: canon-backport skill + retro dual-proposal + phase-9 gate (STORY-1003)'
+   git -C .sdlc push
+   ```
+
+   This pushes all three skill files into the `.sdlc` submodule remote so all agents
+   pick them up on their next session start.
+
+5. **Bump the submodule reference in tech-dev-agents and deploy**
+
+   ```bash
+   git add .sdlc
+   git commit -m 'bump .sdlc submodule: canon-backport + retro dual-proposal + phase-9 gate (STORY-1003)'
+   git push
+   ./deployment/vm/push-code.sh all
+   ```
+
+   This updates the submodule pointer so the new `.sdlc` commit is tracked, then
+   deploys to all agent VMs so their skill directories resolve all three updated skills.
+
+## Verification
+
+After deploying, test in a fresh Claude Code session:
+
+**canon-backport:**
+```
+/canon-backport STORY-1003
+```
+Expected: Claude reads the skill, locates `../gc-data-v2`, reads relevant platform files,
+and either writes a `canon-gap.yaml` or reports "No canon gaps identified."
+
+**retro (gc-data-v2 companion):**
+Run `/retro` on an epic that has at least one `canon-gap.yaml` file in a story folder.
+Expected: Claude generates both `retro-proposal.yaml` AND `retro-proposal-gc-data-v2.yaml`.
+
+**phase-9 gate:**
+Run `/phase-9` on any story.
+Expected: Claude answers Q1, Q2, and Q3 in `refinement-report.md` under
+`## Phase 9 Gate Answers` before proceeding to the Workflow section.
+
+## Rollback
+
+If any step fails:
+
+- **Submodule push fails:** `git -C .sdlc reset HEAD~1 && git -C .sdlc checkout -- .`
+  to undo local changes, then re-check your push access to the submodule remote.
+- **Retro skill regressed:** Restore from git: `git -C .sdlc show HEAD~1:skills/retro/SKILL.md > .sdlc/skills/retro/SKILL.md`
+  then commit the restore inside `.sdlc`.
+- **Phase-9 skill regressed:** Same pattern as retro rollback above.
+- **Skills not resolving after deploy:** Re-run `./deployment/vm/push-code.sh all` —
+  the skills are content-only and have no runtime impact if temporarily absent.
