+# STORY-1003 — Feature Specification
+
+**Phase:** 6 (Design)
+**Scope:** medium
+**Phase path:** 1 → 6 → 7 → 8 → Done
+
+---
+
+## Overview
+
+This story delivers three tightly-coupled SDLC skill enhancements that close the canon-drift
+feedback loop across the tech-dev-agents → gc-data-v2/platform pipeline:
+
+1. **`canon-backport` skill (new)** — When a story's implementation diverges from platform
+   documentation in `gc-data-v2/platform/`, this skill drafts the backport proposal.
+2. **`retro` skill (patched)** — `/retro` now emits a companion proposal file
+   `retro-proposal-gc-data-v2.yaml` alongside the existing `retro-proposal.yaml`.
+3. **`phase-9` skill (patched)** — Phase 9 (Refinement) now starts with a mandatory
+   3-question gate that forces the worker to identify residual gaps before polishing.
+
+All three are content-only (markdown) skill files. No runtime code is added. The deploy
+path is the same as STORY-1004: files land in `features/story-1003-canon-backport-retro/skills/`,
+MANUAL-STEPS.md tells Mark to copy them into `.sdlc/skills/`.
+
+---
+
+## 1. canon-backport Skill Design
+
+### Trigger
+
+The skill is invoked manually by the story worker or by `complete-story` as a suggested
+next action when a canon gap is detected:
+
+```
+/canon-backport                        # guided: Claude asks for story ID and gap description
+/canon-backport STORY-NNNN             # run for a specific story
+/canon-backport STORY-NNNN --auto      # non-interactive: Claude scans and drafts without prompts
+```
+
+### Inputs
+
+| Input | Source | Notes |
+|-------|--------|-------|
+| Story ID | Argument or current story in `.project` | Used to locate `features/<story-folder>/` |
+| gc-data-v2 path | Env or default `../gc-data-v2` | Relative to workspace root |
+| Platform files | `gc-data-v2/platform/` | The canonical documentation |
+
+### Steps
+
+1. **Locate story folder** — Resolve `features/<story-folder>/` from the story ID.
+2. **Read platform docs** — Scan `gc-data-v2/platform/` for docs relevant to this story's
+   domain (ingestion-patterns.md, landing-to-bronze.md, dbt-conventions.md, etc.). Use the
+   story's seed.md / feature-spec.md domain keywords to select which docs to read.
+3. **Identify gaps** — Compare the story's implementation approach (from feature-spec.md,
+   code review, or direct code scan) against the platform documentation. Flag:
+   - Patterns used in the implementation not yet in the docs (additive gap)
+   - Patterns in the docs that the implementation deviated from (deviation gap)
+   - Patterns the implementation improved upon (upstream opportunity)
+4. **Draft canon-gap.yaml** — Write
+   `features/<story-folder>/canon-gap.yaml` with the YAML schema defined in the seed.
+5. **Draft PR description** — Write a human-readable PR description for the `gc-data-v2`
+   repo that describes each gap, the proposed documentation addition, and the evidence.
+   Emit to stdout for Mark to copy into a `gh pr create` command.
+6. **STOP** — Do not `git push` or `gh pr create` automatically.
+
+### Boundaries
+
+- Read-only access to `gc-data-v2/` — never writes to it
+- Drafts only — the skill produces a YAML file and a PR description, not an actual PR
+- Does not modify `.sdlc/` or any file outside `features/<story-folder>/`
+- If `gc-data-v2/` is not present at `../gc-data-v2`, emit a warning with the path and stop
+
+### Output Format
+
+**`features/<story-folder>/canon-gap.yaml`:**
+
+```yaml
+# canon-gap.yaml — generated by /canon-backport
+version: 1
+story: STORY-NNNN
+date: YYYY-MM-DD
+repo: gc-data-v2
+gaps:
+  - id: CG-001
+    platform_file: platform/ingestion-patterns.md
+    type: additive      # additive | deviation | upstream-opportunity
+    severity: Medium    # High | Medium | Low
+    finding: "Brief description of the pattern gap"
+    proposed_addition: |
+      ## Pattern Name — <description>
+      ...markdown content to add to the platform file...
+    evidence:
+      - "features/STORY-NNNN/feature-spec.md: describes pattern X"
+      - "src/path/file.py:42: implements pattern X"
+```
+
+**PR description (stdout):**
+
+```markdown
+## Canon Backport: STORY-NNNN → gc-data-v2/platform
+
+### Summary
+N canon gaps found during STORY-NNNN implementation.
+
+### Proposed Changes
+[One section per gap with finding + proposed text]
+
+### Evidence
+[Pointers back to story artifacts]
+
+### How to open this PR
+gh pr create --repo hpi-gorillacommerce/gc-data-v2 --title "canon: backport STORY-NNNN patterns" --body "..."
+```
+
+---
+
+## 2. retro Skill Patch Design
+
+### Change
+
+The patched retro skill adds **Step 8a** between the existing Step 7 (export proposal file)
+and Step 8 (present to user):
+
+> **Step 8a — Export gc-data-v2 companion proposal (NEW)**
+> Scan all story folders for `canon-gap.yaml` files. If any exist:
+> - Aggregate all gaps into `features/<epic-folder>/retro-proposal-gc-data-v2.yaml`
+> - Format mirrors `retro-proposal.yaml` but `target_file` references `gc-data-v2/platform/<file>`
+> If no `canon-gap.yaml` files found, emit a note and skip this step.
+
+### New section added to SKILL.md
+
+```markdown
+## gc-data-v2 Companion Proposal
+
+When canon-gap.yaml files are present in any story folder for this epic, `/retro` emits
+a second proposal file: `features/<epic-folder>/retro-proposal-gc-data-v2.yaml`.
+
+This companion proposal:
+- Contains only platform-documentation improvement proposals
+- Targets files in `gc-data-v2/platform/`
+- Uses the same YAML schema as retro-proposal.yaml (with `target_file` pointing to
+  gc-data-v2/platform/ files instead of SDLC framework files)
+- Is safe to share with the data platform team (no proprietary business logic)
+
+### Companion Format
+
+```yaml
+# retro-proposal-gc-data-v2.yaml
+version: 1
+project: <project-name>
+epic: <epic-name>
+date: YYYY-MM-DD
+target_repo: gc-data-v2
+metrics:
+  stories_with_canon_gaps: N
+  total_gaps: N
+proposals:
+  - id: CG-001
+    story: STORY-NNNN
+    finding: "Pattern X used in story but not in platform docs"
+    category: platform/ingestion-patterns.md
+    severity: Medium
+    target_file: platform/ingestion-patterns.md
+    action: "Add Pattern X to Ingestion Patterns"
+    proposed_text: |
+      ## Pattern X — <name>
+      ...
+    evidence:
+      - "features/STORY-NNNN/canon-gap.yaml"
+```
+```
+
+### Patching strategy
+
+The patched `retro/SKILL.md` is the source file with:
+1. Step 8a added between current steps 7 and 8
+2. The `## gc-data-v2 Companion Proposal` section added after `## Proposal File Format`
+3. All existing content preserved verbatim
+
+---
+
+## 3. phase-9 Skill Patch Design
+
+### Change
+
+A `## 3-Question Gate (REQUIRED)` section is added **before** the `## Workflow` section.
+
+### 3-Question Gate Content
+
+```markdown
+## 3-Question Gate (REQUIRED)
+
+Before writing a single line of refinement code, answer these three questions.
+Write answers in `refinement-report.md` under a `## Phase 9 Gate Answers` section.
+Only proceed to the Workflow below once all three are answered.
+
+**Q1 — Open Code Review Findings**
+List every finding from `features/<story-folder>/code-review.md` (Phase 8b) that was
+not fully resolved during Phase 8 implementation. Mark each as:
+- `RESOLVED in Phase 8`: brief note on how
+- `DEFERRED to Phase 9`: this becomes a mandatory work item
+- `WONTFIX`: brief justification
+
+If Phase 8b was skipped (small scope), write "Phase 8b skipped — no findings."
+
+**Q2 — Test Coverage Assessment**
+Report current test coverage percentage (run `python -m pytest --cov` or equivalent).
+List every module or file below 80% coverage with its current %. These become
+mandatory coverage targets for Phase 9.
+
+If coverage tooling is unavailable, write: "Coverage unavailable — manual audit:"
+then list the 3 most critical untested code paths.
+
+**Q3 — Canon Gap Check**
+Did this story's implementation diverge from any `gc-data-v2/platform/` patterns?
+- If yes: run `/canon-backport STORY-NNNN` now and append the output summary here.
+- If no: write "No canon gaps identified."
+- If gc-data-v2 is not applicable to this story: write "gc-data-v2 not in scope."
+
+**Gate decision:** Do NOT proceed to the Workflow until all three questions have
+written answers. If any answer requires investigation, do that investigation first.
+```
+
+---
+
+## File Layout
+
+```
+features/story-1003-canon-backport-retro/
+  seed.md                              ← Phase 1 (exists)
+  feature-spec.md                      ← Phase 6 (this file)
+  MANUAL-STEPS.md                      ← Phase 8
+  skills/
+    canon-backport/
+      SKILL.md                         ← Phase 8 (new skill)
+    retro/
+      SKILL.md                         ← Phase 8 (patched from .sdlc/skills/retro/SKILL.md)
+    phase-9/
+      SKILL.md                         ← Phase 8 (patched from .sdlc/skills/phase-9/SKILL.md)
+
+tests/skills/
+  test_1003_canon_backport_retro.py    ← Phase 7 (RED) → Phase 8 (GREEN)
+```
+
+---
+
+## Test Plan (Phase 7 preview)
+
+| Group | Target file | Tests |
+|-------|------------|-------|
+| A | canon-backport/SKILL.md | 7 — frontmatter, when-to-run, steps (4 sub-steps), YAML format, boundaries |
+| B | retro/SKILL.md patch | 6 — original content preserved, step-8a added, companion format section, gc-data-v2 yaml schema |
+| C | phase-9/SKILL.md patch | 4 — original content preserved, gate section present, 3 questions present, gate-decision language |
+| D | MANUAL-STEPS.md | 3 — copy instructions, git submodule reference, numbered steps |
+
+Total: 20 tests
+
+---
+
+## Risks & Mitigations
+
+| Risk | Mitigation |
+|------|-----------|
+| Retro patch accidentally drops existing steps | Test B2 asserts all original numbered steps are still present |
+| phase-9 patch breaks existing workflow | Test C2 asserts `## Workflow` section still present and unchanged |
+| canon-backport accidentally pushes to gc-data-v2 | Boundaries section explicitly states skill is draft-only; tested in A6 |
+| MANUAL-STEPS.md incomplete | Test D3 asserts at least 4 numbered steps with copy + git commands |
+
