+---
+name: canon-backport
+description: >
+  Draft a backport proposal when a story's implementation diverges from gc-data-v2/platform/
+  documentation. Produces canon-gap.yaml in the story folder and a human-readable PR
+  description for the data platform team. Draft-only — never pushes automatically.
+triggers:
+  - canon backport
+  - canon gap
+  - backport to platform
+  - gc-data-v2 gap
+  - platform docs gap
+  - canon drift
+  - backport pattern
+---
+
+# canon-backport — Platform Documentation Backport
+
+Draft a proposal to synchronise `gc-data-v2/platform/` with patterns discovered or
+refined during a story's implementation. Produces a `canon-gap.yaml` file and a
+human-readable PR description for the data-platform team.
+
+This skill is **draft-only** — it never pushes to `gc-data-v2` automatically.
+
+## When to run
+
+Run this skill at the end of a story — during Phase 8 implementation or when
+`/complete-story` is wrapping up — if any of the following are true:
+
+- The story introduced a new ingestion pattern, auth flow, or platform integration
+  not yet documented in `gc-data-v2/platform/`.
+- The implementation improved upon or deviated from an existing platform pattern.
+- A Phase 8b code review finding identified a documentation gap in the platform.
+- `/retro` flagged this story's epic as having platform documentation debt.
+
+> **Phase 9 workers:** the 3-question gate in `/phase-9` asks you to run
+> `/canon-backport STORY-NNNN` if any canon gaps were identified. Do that here
+> and paste the summary into your Q3 answer.
+
+## Usage
+
+```
+/canon-backport                        # guided: Claude asks for story ID + gap description
+/canon-backport STORY-NNNN             # run for a specific story
+/canon-backport STORY-NNNN --auto      # non-interactive: Claude scans and drafts without prompts
+```
+
+## Steps
+
+1. **Locate story folder**
+   Resolve `features/<story-folder>/` from the story ID (match by `STORY-NNNN` prefix
+   in the `features/` directory). If the folder is not found, stop and ask the user to
+   confirm the story ID.
+
+2. **Read platform docs**
+   Locate the `gc-data-v2/` repo at `../gc-data-v2` relative to the current workspace
+   root. If the path does not exist, emit:
+   ```
+   ⚠ gc-data-v2 not found at ../gc-data-v2
+   Set GC_DATA_V2_PATH env var to override, or check out gc-data-v2 alongside this repo.
+   ```
+   Then stop. Do not proceed without the platform docs.
+
+   Read the platform files most likely relevant to this story:
+   - `gc-data-v2/platform/ingestion-patterns.md`
+   - `gc-data-v2/platform/landing-to-bronze.md`
+   - `gc-data-v2/platform/dbt-conventions.md`
+   - `gc-data-v2/platform/airflow-conventions.md`
+   - `gc-data-v2/platform/auth-patterns.md`
+   - Any others referenced in the story's `feature-spec.md` or `seed.md`
+
+3. **Identify gaps**
+   Compare the story's implementation approach (from `features/<story-folder>/feature-spec.md`,
+   `features/<story-folder>/code-review.md`, or direct code scan of the story branch)
+   against the platform docs read in Step 2. For each divergence, classify as:
+
+   - `additive` — Story used a pattern not yet in platform docs (add it)
+   - `deviation` — Story deviated from a documented pattern (document the reason or update the pattern)
+   - `upstream-opportunity` — Story improved a pattern enough that the docs should be updated
+
+4. **Draft canon-gap.yaml**
+   Write `features/<story-folder>/canon-gap.yaml` with the schema defined below.
+   If no gaps are found, write a minimal file with an empty `gaps:` list and a comment
+   noting the story was reviewed and found no gaps.
+
+5. **Draft PR description**
+   Write a human-readable PR description to stdout. Include:
+   - One section per gap (gap ID, platform file, proposed change)
+   - Evidence pointers to story artifacts (seed.md, feature-spec.md, code lines)
+   - The `gh pr create` command for Mark to copy-paste
+
+6. **STOP**
+   Do not `git push`, `git commit` in `gc-data-v2`, or `gh pr create` automatically.
+   Present the canon-gap.yaml summary and the PR description for human review.
+
+## Canon Gap YAML Format
+
+Write to `features/<story-folder>/canon-gap.yaml`:
+
+```yaml
+# canon-gap.yaml — generated by /canon-backport
+# This file is draft-only. Review before opening a PR to gc-data-v2.
+version: 1
+story: STORY-NNNN
+date: YYYY-MM-DD
+repo: gc-data-v2
+reviewed: false          # set to true after Mark reviews the proposed additions
+gaps:
+  - id: CG-001
+    platform_file: platform/ingestion-patterns.md
+    type: additive        # additive | deviation | upstream-opportunity
+    severity: Medium      # High | Medium | Low
+    finding: |
+      One-sentence description of the pattern gap.
+    proposed_addition: |
+      ## Pattern Name — <description>
+
+      <markdown content to add to the platform file>
+    evidence:
+      - "features/STORY-NNNN/feature-spec.md: describes approach"
+      - "features/STORY-NNNN/feature-spec.md:42: specific reference"
+```
+
+**Severity guide:**
+
+| Severity | Meaning |
+|----------|---------|
+| High | Gap causes new workers to implement incorrectly if they follow the docs |
+| Medium | Docs miss a useful pattern that workers would benefit from knowing |
+| Low | Minor improvement or clarification |
+
+## PR Description Template (stdout)
+
+After generating `canon-gap.yaml`, emit this to stdout for Mark:
+
+```
+## Canon Backport: STORY-NNNN → gc-data-v2/platform
+
+N gap(s) identified during STORY-NNNN implementation.
+
+### Gap CG-001 — <platform_file>
+**Type:** additive | deviation | upstream-opportunity
+**Severity:** High | Medium | Low
+
+**Finding:** <one-sentence description>
+
+**Proposed change to <platform_file>:**
+```markdown
+<proposed_addition>
+```
+
+**Evidence:** <evidence list>
+
+---
+
+### To open this PR (copy-paste):
+gh pr create \
+  --repo hpi-gorillacommerce/gc-data-v2 \
+  --title "canon: backport STORY-NNNN patterns to platform docs" \
+  --body "..."
+```
+
+## Boundaries
+
+- **Read-only access to gc-data-v2.** This skill reads `../gc-data-v2/platform/` files
+  but does NOT write to them. It never creates commits in `gc-data-v2`.
+- **Draft only.** The skill only drafts proposals — it does not push to `gc-data-v2`,
+  does not open PRs automatically, and does not modify `.sdlc/` in any way.
+- **Story folder only.** The only file written by this skill is
+  `features/<story-folder>/canon-gap.yaml`. No other files are created or modified.
+- **No business logic.** The `canon-gap.yaml` and PR description contain only
+  documentation improvements — no proprietary pipeline code, source credentials, or
+  business rules that should not be in a shared repo.
+- **Graceful absence.** If `gc-data-v2/` is not present at `../gc-data-v2`, warn and
+  stop — do not guess paths or scan the whole filesystem.
+
+## Integration with complete-story
+
+When `/complete-story` runs for a story that includes data-platform work, it should
+suggest running `/canon-backport STORY-NNNN` before fully marking the story done.
+The suggestion is advisory — not a hard gate. The story can be marked complete even if
+`canon-gap.yaml` is not present, but the platform docs lag is noted.
+
+## Integration with retro
+
+`/retro` scans all story folders for `canon-gap.yaml` files. If any are found, it
+aggregates them into a `retro-proposal-gc-data-v2.yaml` companion file. This means
+running `/canon-backport` on each story during Phase 8/9 pays dividends at retro time:
+the platform documentation improvement is automatically surfaced at the epic level.
