+# STORY-1010 — Feature Spec (Phase 6)
+
+## 1. Registry Data Model
+
+```python
+@dataclass(frozen=True, slots=True)
+class Fallback:
+    skill_name: str
+    sql_template: str          # parameterized SQL ($1, $2 etc.)
+    runbook_url: str           # placeholder OK if page is in STORY-1015/1016
+    description: str           # one-sentence operator-facing explanation
+    required_params: list[str] # e.g. ["repo", "hours"]
+```
+
+**Registration mechanism:** module-level dict `REGISTRY: dict[str, Fallback]` populated by `register_fallback()` calls at module load time. No decorator — plain function calls are clearer for a fixed set of 5 skills.
+
+**Lookup:** `get_fallback(skill_name) -> Fallback | None`
+
+**Render:** `render_fallback(skill_name, **params) -> dict` returns `{"skill_name": ..., "sql": ..., "runbook_url": ..., "description": ..., "params_used": {...}}`. The `sql` field has `$1`, `$2` replaced with the provided param values (for display). If params are missing, template is returned raw with `$N` placeholders.
+
+## 2. The 5 Initial Entries
+
+### `/requeue-failed`
+- **SQL:** `UPDATE dispatch_state_current SET state = 'enqueued', updated_at = NOW() WHERE state = 'failed' AND job_id IN (SELECT job_id FROM dispatch_jobs WHERE repo = $1 AND created_at > NOW() - INTERVAL '$2 hours');`
+- **Params:** `["repo", "hours"]`
+- **Runbook:** `https://tech-gc-knowledgebase.gorillacommerce.ai/wiki/runbooks/requeue-failed.md`
+- **Description:** Requeue all failed jobs for a given repo within the last N hours.
+
+### `/dispatch-recovery`
+- **SQL:** `UPDATE dispatch_state_current SET state = 'enqueued', updated_at = NOW() WHERE state = 'dead_letter' AND job_id IN (SELECT job_id FROM dispatch_jobs WHERE repo = $1 AND story_id = $2);`
+- **Params:** `["repo", "story_id"]`
+- **Runbook:** `https://tech-gc-knowledgebase.gorillacommerce.ai/wiki/runbooks/dispatch-recovery.md`
+- **Description:** Recover a dead-lettered dispatch job by story ID back to enqueued state.
+
+### `/release-stale-claim`
+- **SQL:** `DELETE FROM dispatch_leases WHERE job_id IN (SELECT job_id FROM dispatch_leases WHERE expires_at < NOW()) RETURNING job_id;`
+- **Params:** `[]`
+- **Runbook:** `https://tech-gc-knowledgebase.gorillacommerce.ai/wiki/runbooks/release-stale-claim.md`
+- **Description:** Release all expired lease claims so stalled jobs return to the claimable pool.
+
+### `/dead-letter-purge`
+- **SQL:** `DELETE FROM dispatch_v2_events WHERE job_id IN (SELECT job_id FROM dispatch_state_current WHERE state = 'dead_letter' AND updated_at < NOW() - INTERVAL '$1 days'); DELETE FROM dispatch_state_current WHERE state = 'dead_letter' AND updated_at < NOW() - INTERVAL '$1 days';`
+- **Params:** `["retention_days"]`
+- **Runbook:** `https://tech-gc-knowledgebase.gorillacommerce.ai/wiki/runbooks/dead-letter-purge.md`
+- **Description:** Purge dead-lettered jobs older than N days (events + state rows).
+
+### `/force-claim`
+- **SQL:** `INSERT INTO dispatch_leases (job_id, lease_token, expires_at, claimed_by) VALUES ($1::uuid, gen_random_uuid(), NOW() + INTERVAL '30 minutes', $2) ON CONFLICT (job_id) DO UPDATE SET lease_token = gen_random_uuid(), expires_at = NOW() + INTERVAL '30 minutes', claimed_by = $2 RETURNING lease_token, expires_at;`
+- **Params:** `["job_id", "claimed_by"]`
+- **Runbook:** `https://tech-gc-knowledgebase.gorillacommerce.ai/wiki/runbooks/force-claim.md`
+- **Description:** Force-claim a specific job, overriding any existing lease.
+
+## 3. `transition()` Gate Semantics
+
+Decision tree inside `DispatchV2Service.transition()`:
+
+```
+if event_type != "submitted":
+    → pass through (no pr_number check)
+else:
+    # existing submitted → in_review guardrail runs first (lines 579-617)
+    # THEN: new enforcement gate
+    if pr_number IS NOT NULL on job row (or was just set via event_data):
+        → pass (PR linked)
+    else:
+        created_at = dispatch_jobs.created_at for this job_id
+        rollout_ts = parse(os.environ.get("OPS_PR_NUMBER_ENFORCEMENT_ROLLOUT", "2099-01-01T00:00:00Z"))
+        if created_at > rollout_ts:
+            → raise InvalidEventDataError(422):
+              "in_review requires pr_number — backfill via /api/dispatch/v2/{job_id}/set-pr-number"
+        else:
+            → allow (legacy dispatch, sweeper will backfill)
+```
+
+Note: The existing guardrail at lines 579-617 already handles the `submitted` event type and enforces PR linkage. The NEW gate applies the `OPS_PR_NUMBER_ENFORCEMENT_ROLLOUT` timestamp check so that new dispatches are hard-blocked while legacy ones pass through to the sweeper.
+
+**Default rollout timestamp:** `2099-01-01T00:00:00Z` (effectively disabled until ops sets the env var).
+
+## 4. `set-pr-number` Endpoint Contract
+
+**Route:** `POST /api/dispatch/v2/{job_id}/set-pr-number`
+
+**Payload:**
+```json
+{"pr_number": 123}
+```
+
+**Response:**
+- `200 {"job_id": "...", "pr_number": 123}` — first call or idempotent repeat.
+- `409 {"detail": "pr_number conflict: existing=123, submitted=456"}` — different value already set.
+- `404 {"detail": "job_id not found"}` — no such job.
+
+**SQL:**
+```sql
+UPDATE dispatch_jobs
+SET pr_number = $2
+WHERE job_id = $1::uuid AND pr_number IS NULL
+RETURNING job_id;
+-- If 0 rows affected, check if existing matches (200) or conflicts (409).
+```
+
+## 5. Observability
+
+- Log line on every legacy backfill: `pr_link_backfill: legacy_dispatch story_id=<sid>`
+  (Added in `self_healing.py` — minimal edit to `_pr_link_backfill_tick`)
+- Log line on gate block: `pr_number_gate: blocked job_id=<jid> created_at=<ts>`
+- Log line on fallback render: `ops_fallback_render: skill=<name>`
+
+## 6. Test Fixtures
+
+- **"new" dispatch:** `created_at = datetime(2026, 5, 19, tzinfo=timezone.utc)` (after rollout)
+- **"legacy" dispatch:** `created_at = datetime(2026, 5, 1, tzinfo=timezone.utc)` (before rollout)
+- **Rollout timestamp:** `OPS_PR_NUMBER_ENFORCEMENT_ROLLOUT=2026-05-18T00:00:00Z`
+- Both fixtures reused across gate tests + sweeper tests.
